From 537414c8852ac125bb74c37c50d45dbe8b053b9c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: stephan-xyz <stephan@zehrer.net>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 20:57:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Free the last partial record when a file is truncated or
 removed

truncate_node_inner deallocated the records from size.div_ceil(record)
up to old_size / record. The upper end rounds down, so the last,
partly filled record of the old size was never freed. Removing a file
truncates it to 0, so every removed file lost its last record: a file
smaller than one record (up to 128 KiB) kept all its blocks allocated,
a larger one its tail. The space stayed lost after a remount.

On a 222 MiB root, installing and removing vim (2223 files, mostly
small) lost about 12 MiB each time, and the root was full after seven
rounds (redox-rpi issue #197).

Round the upper end up, like the lower end.
---
 src/transaction.rs | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/transaction.rs b/src/transaction.rs
index 2fc5594..0ce0fe0 100644
--- a/src/transaction.rs
+++ b/src/transaction.rs
@@ -1850,7 +1850,7 @@ impl<'a, D: Disk> Transaction<'a, D> {
         } else if !node.data().has_inline_data() {
             // Deallocate records
             for record in
-                (size.div_ceil(record_level.bytes())..old_size / record_level.bytes()).rev()
+                (size.div_ceil(record_level.bytes())..old_size.div_ceil(record_level.bytes())).rev()
             {
                 self.remove_node_record_ptr(node, record)?;
             }
-- 
